headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
  X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}
  Accept-Language: {{acceptLanguage}}
  X-Correlation-Id: {{$guid}}
  Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
}

docs {
  Settings (gateway and API addresses, GM.Identity's gateway and sign-in, tenant, page size, language) live in the
  Local environment — select it before running. Every call goes through the gateway, as a client's would.

  The gateway needs a GM.Identity sign-in: run Auth/Sign In first (with GM.Identity.Samples running). It saves
  accessToken, which every request sends as a bearer token; the gateway sets the caller's user from it.

  Every request also names the tenant (X-Tenant-Id), so the files you upload belong to that tenant and only it sees
  them. A session bound to another tenant gets 403. Leave tenantId empty to work in the shared "public" space.

  Every request also sends a fresh X-Correlation-Id and Idempotency-Key; Files/Upload File Again reuses Upload
  File's key to show a retry being replayed.

  Run Files in order: Upload File saves fileId, which the later requests use. The files uploaded are in sample-files/.

  Values the scripts save (accessToken, fileId, retryKey) go into the Local environment as unsaved, in-memory values.
}
